<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raymond III of Tripoli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1140–<a href="/years/1187">1187</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raymond III was count of Tripoli from 1152 and, through his wife <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eschiva-of-bures">Eschiva of Bures</a>, prince of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galilee">Galilee</a>. He was regent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a> twice and a rival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guy-of-lusignan">Guy of Lusignan</a>. In 1187 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberias">Tiberias</a>, and the royal army marching to relieve it was destroyed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hattin">Hattin</a>. Raymond escaped but died later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raymond-iii-of-tripoli.jpg" alt="Raymond III of Tripoli" width="320" height="344" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author from northern France · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raymond_III_of_Tripoli_named_regent.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
